svc('ma-it-due-diligence', 'M&A IT Due Diligence',
    title="IT and Technology Due Diligence for M&A | Dividend IT",
    meta="IT due diligence for buyers, investors and sellers: a clear picture of systems, risks, licensing and integration cost before the deal is done.",
    card_desc="A clear picture of the technology you are buying, before you sign.",
    h1="M&amp;A <em>IT due diligence</em>",
    lead="Technology problems found after completion are expensive, and they are yours. IT due diligence shows you what you are really acquiring while it can still change the price. You get a risk and liability report covering systems, costs, licensing, people and security, plus a hundred-day plan for after completion.",
    glance=[('Best for', 'Buyers, investors and owners preparing to sell'),
            ('You get', 'A risk and liability report and a 100-day plan'),
            ('Looks at', 'Systems, costs, licensing, people and security'),
            ('Timing', 'Before signing, while it can still affect the price')],
    problem_h="What exactly are you buying?",
    problem=[
        "A business can look healthy in the accounts and be held together by a server that went out of support years ago, software nobody is licensed for and one long-serving employee who is the only person who understands how it all works.",
        "None of that appears in a financial model. All of it becomes the buyer's cost on completion.",
        "In our experience, a buyer's technology diligence comes down to four questions: <strong>is it secure, is it documented and licensed, does it depend on one person, and is the spending efficient and correctly treated?</strong> We answer all four with evidence."],
    included_h="What we examine",
    included=[
        ("Infrastructure and systems", "What technology the business runs on, how old it is and what will need replacing."),
        ("Risk and liability", "End-of-life systems, unlicensed software, data protection gaps and supplier lock-in that could affect value."),
        ("Key-person dependency", "Whether critical knowledge sits in one head, and what happens if that person leaves."),
        ("Cost quality", "Whether technology spending is efficient, predictable and treated correctly in the accounts."),
        ("Integration complexity", "How hard and how costly it will be to combine the target's technology with yours."),
        ("A 100-day plan", "A ready-to-run plan for the first hundred days after completion.")],
    steps_h="How it fits your deal timeline",
    steps=[
        ("Scope", "We agree the questions that matter for this deal with you and your advisers."),
        ("Investigate", "We review documents, speak to key people and examine the evidence."),
        ("Report", "You get findings ranked by their effect on value, with costs attached."),
        ("Plan", "We leave you with a 100-day plan for after completion.")],
    value_h="Findings you can negotiate with",
    value_intro="A diligence report is only useful if it changes a decision. Ours is written to be used at the negotiating table.",
    value=[
        ("For buyers: ", "price the real cost of the technology you are inheriting, and avoid surprises after completion."),
        ("For sellers: ", "find and fix the issues first, so the buyer's adviser has nothing to chip the price with."),
        ("For investors: ", "an independent view of whether the technology can support the growth plan.")],
    fit=(["You are acquiring or investing in a business",
          "You plan to sell within one to three years and want to be ready",
          "The target relies heavily on its systems to operate",
          "Your advisers want specialist technology input"],
         ["The deal has already completed. An <a href=\"/it-strategy\">IT strategy review</a> is the better starting point",
          "You need legal or financial due diligence. We complement those advisers and do not replace them"]),
    faqs=[
        ("What is IT due diligence?", "It is an independent assessment of a company's technology carried out before a merger, acquisition or investment. It covers systems, costs, contracts, licensing, security, people and how difficult integration will be."),
        ("What is the difference between IT due diligence and technology due diligence?", "They are used interchangeably for most businesses. Technology due diligence sometimes implies a deeper look at software products a company has built. For businesses that use technology and do not sell it, they are the same exercise."),
        ("What does IT due diligence look for?", "Security record and incident history, documentation and licence compliance, key-person dependency and the quality of technology spending, along with the likely cost of integration."),
        ("We are selling. How does this help us?", "A seller who commissions the review first can fix issues on their own timetable and present clean evidence. That supports the valuation and shortens the buyer's process. Our guide to <a href=\"/exit-value\">realising value at exit</a> explains why it matters.")],
    related=['ma-cyber-due-diligence', 'ma-it-strategy', 'exit-value'],
    cta_h="Know what you are buying, or selling.",
    cta_p="A confidential 20-minute call about your deal, your timeline and a sensible scope.",
),
